\begin{equation}
\label{harnackinequality}
R(x_2,t_2)\geq
\exp\left(-\frac{d_{t_1}^2(x_1,x_2)}{2(t_2-t_1)}\right)R(x_1,t_1).
\end{equation}
For $n=2$, the denominator in the exponential may be replaced by
$4(t_2-t_1)$; if $R(x_2,t_2)=0$, then $g(t)$ is flat for all $t$.

